From 77117020768f5e9edb7b82fb8b273734c2b09fe6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:25:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(widget): ReleaseRenderers frees a replaced tree's
 renderers at once

The renderer cache keeps the renderer of every widget until it expires, a
minute after the widget was last painted, and only DestroyRenderer, which is
internal, frees one earlier. An app that rebuilds part of a screen on every
change therefore holds a minute of old screens: their renderers, the canvas
of each object and their textures. Measured in the Sytue suite, a calendar
month repaint left 1.3 MB behind each time (+79 MiB after 60).

widget.ReleaseRenderers(old, kept...) frees at once what the cache holds for
old and everything it contains: it destroys the cached renderers of its
widgets (calling Destroy), forgets the canvas of each object and marks their
textures as expired, so the next texture clean on the painter's thread frees
them. Objects that are also in one of the kept trees, which is where an app
that rebuilds only part of a screen leaves the pieces it reuses, are left
alone with everything they contain. Only containers and existing renderers
are walked: no renderer is created. A released widget that is shown again
simply gets a new renderer.

New tests: TestReleaseRenderers_FreesTheReplacedTreeAndKeepsTheReused and
_CreatesNoRenderer (widget), TestReleaseTree_FreesNowWhatWouldExpireLater and
_CreatesNoRenderer (internal/cache).

